{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see","id":77541,"title":"Books you would like to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-23T01:58:38-08:00","id":77541,"title":"Books you would like to see?","content":"I'd bet money that Hunter: the Vigil is the most popular limited-run game, behind Changeling. While there's nothing beyond Mortal Remains on the schedule for 2014 (which is cause enough for celebration), I have my fingers crossed for it to grab enough attention to justify more books in 2015. Hunter's a very versatile game, and could easily support a further run of supplements. What would you like to see?<br /> <br /> At the very top of my list is a book like Ancient Mysteries/Ancient Bloodline, one that gives snapshots of the Vigil across the ages. As long as there's been humanity, monsters have preyed on man, and hunters have stood to oppose them. Throw out five or six small settings and show off some Compacts and Conspiracies that no longer exist in the modern day. A <i>Vigil for Rome</i> portion with a focus on the Aves Minerva and some monsters that are extinct in modern nights, and do the same for any other time that stands out.<br /> <br /> <i>Mortal Remains</i> might address this, but a small book with a focus on monster-building would be wonderful. Lots of new Dread Powers and templates for things far stranger than the usual critters that have their own games about them. This would be as good a place as any to potentially throw in aliens or more Christian demons, along with Lovecraftian beasties and their cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T03:33:42-08:00","id":77564,"title":"","content":"Most of the books I want to see I consider writing myself, however.<br /> <br /> I don't have anything against fighting monsters, but I've always been more interested in Vigil as an investigative / social game. There's support for this, Null Mysteriis, but I want more. So the first book I'd like to see is Hunter: Bread Winners.<br /> <br /> This is a book about Hunters with normal lives, and something in that normal life convinced them to see out the supernatural. Joe Average knows monsters exist but he pretends they don't, like most people in the World of Darkness, then one day he discovers the factory is about to be offshored, he stops pretending the monsters aren't real and looks for a magical solution. What will it cost, and what will the Union Cell in his factory (that he knows nothing about) think?<br /> <br /> A chapter on storytelling: why would an average person decide (decide is key, IMO the difference between a Hunter and a blue book mortal is that the Hunter could so easily have ignored the supernatural but at a crucial moment they decided not to) to seek out magic to solve an issue in regular life. Then advice on how to build cool stories for this. Some <i>basic</i> talk about various solutions, but mostly a stop-gap if you don't have other books that cover the monsters in more details.<br /> <br /> A chapter on mechanics, I'm thinking of diving into the Professions. I'm thinking of advice on what they can do with their contacts, skills, and maybe a Merit or Tactic that's based on their training.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second book I'd like to see is Witch Finders, done right. Unlike the Awakened (who are different on a metaphysical level) most Witches are just humans with magic. I'd like too really see that, for example The Union sees Witches as &quot;immediate trouble, propsoened trouble, never friends&quot;. I want to see friends, what happens when a local witch (with no combat experience but a decent reputation) knocks on The Unions door and asks for help with a summoning gone wrong? What happens when the Union's community links includes it's witches? What do the Union think of Witches joining a cell, or hunters learning magic. I want to see questions like that answered given equal weight to &quot;why do the unions shoot witches&quot;.<br /> <br /> You could do something like that for other monsters but Witches, being human, are the one where it's needed the most.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Third and most importantly, Hunter: Cults. In fact I'm so enamoured with the concept of this book that a part of me wants to call this Hunter: The Cult Chronciles. Cults is about the following:<br /> <br /> Providing low level antagonists. If you look at Vampire, even a low level Vampire is a serious threat to a Cell of The Union. Cults provides smaller threats that Hunters can face on an even footing, humans with minor blessings from their gods or even no power at all - it by no means the complete picture on low level antagonists but it's a good start.<br /> <br /> Make organisations into organisations. It's more a feeling than a fact, but I get the impression that a typical Tier 3 Hunter game still results in PCs acting like a Tier 1 Cell. They have nifty endowments, and sometimes allies or information, but mostly they're perusing their own Vigil in their own way. Cults will contain advice and mechanics for playing part of a large organisation.<br /> <br /> Complete the picture on morality. Lets face it, Slasher was one of the best books in the WoD. Hunters have always had moral ambiguity and a slide to sociopathy in the corebook thanks to The Code, Slasher completed the picture by showing what's at the bottom of that slide. The moral slide of Conspiracies is also in the corebook, it's time to show what lies at the bottom there too.<br /> <br /> Stuff to investigate. Cults will create lots of sinister secrets and tempting immoral magic, all of which can be used by regular humans. It's one thing investigating a vampire's magic, it's another investigating a cultists magic and knowing that you could steal those secrets yourself. Plus, since cultists are human you really should investigate more than just enough to spot the fangs.<br /> <br /> Less importantly, Gods. Three of the six core Conspiracies are explicitly religiously themed, two of the four supplementary ones also have religious themes. Gods, mythology and religion is extremely important in Hunter, and Cults will give advice for actually including the Gods themselves in your Hunter game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T03:34:54-08:00","id":77565,"title":"","content":"A Throughout the ages book would be awesome<br /> <br /> Hunter's Recongnition Guide pt 2 with stories that weren't easily recognized.<br /> <br /> Night Horrors style book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T05:21:58-08:00","id":77598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=77564#post77564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the books I want to see I consider writing myself, however.<br /> <br /> Providing low level antagonists. If you look at Vampire, even a low level Vampire is a serious threat to a Cell of The Union. Cults provides smaller threats that Hunters can face on an even footing, humans with minor blessings from their gods or even no power at all - it by no means the complete picture on low level antagonists but it's a good start.<br /> <br /> Make organisations into organisations. It's more a feeling than a fact, but I get the impression that a typical Tier 3 Hunter game still results in PCs acting like a Tier 1 Cell. They have nifty endowments, and sometimes allies or information, but mostly they're perusing their own Vigil in their own way. Cults will contain advice and mechanics for playing part of a large organisation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think these two are both essential.<br /> <br /> Regarding the first point: barring the rare zombie invasion or a truly high-power chronicle, many Hunter games take the shape of &quot;bad thing happens, investigation, fight against individual powerful monster.&quot; Some exciting options for less asymetrical opponents would be very welcome. Cults make for an exciting dash of moral grey; Hunters are, at the heart of things, vigilantes with a cause. Does that really entitle you to kill people who are misguided, desperate, or brainwashed?<br /> <br /> The latter is something I really crave. Many of the Tier 3 groups are potential globe-spanning, and yet the average cell is left to their own devices other than someone passing down new Endowments every once in a while. Feeling like a part of a larger, cohesive body is often missing, and something I really enjoy in play. A focus on making sure your VALKYRIE squad has a home base to report to and debriefings to put up with, having your Lucifuge cell make yearly visits to Milan, or your Cheiron acquisitions team filing reports with their supervisor at the tail end of the week would all be most welcome. The greatest asset gained by joining a Compact or Conspiracy is organization, information, and resources; you have people to call on for help, at the cost of following orders and being held responsible for your actions. Stressing this would be really cool.<br /> <br /> Addendum: Something on non-Endowment assets for Tier 2 and 3 play would be really great. Sure, your VALKYRIE cell has Aetheric Rounds in their MP5s, but can they requisition a helicopter or a back-up team? The Union is bound to make friends around town; perhaps one of them is a no-questions-asked surgeon or can get them illegal firearms? This doesn't necessarily have to be enforced by mechanics, but just Storyteller guidelines for making Tier 2 and 3 play feel that much more powerful than just being a lone cell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-23-2014, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T07:06:48-08:00","id":77638,"title":"","content":"I second a book about cults. I didn't like the cults presented in Antagonists. Too mundane and low key for me. I would a book about cults in the same style as Slasher. <br /> Same can be said about Witches. The witches in Witch Finders are still pretty similar to the ones in MtAw, only more simple and less flexible in their powers. I would like a book about witches different from the ones in Mage. Maybe done in the same manner as the Low Magic chapter of Second Sight, only more powerful, because I found the witches in Second Sight too low key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T18:43:37-08:00","id":77964,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a book about building monsters with quick &amp; easy package systems. You pick an Attribute pack like (Brusier, Tank, Rake, Socialite, Leader, Wily, Genius) that have pre-constructed Attributes, then you tack on a Skills Package, &amp; Dread Powers Packages like (Werewolf Bezerker, Vampire Charmer, Vampire Predator, Werewolf Shaman, Undead Titan, Dark Sorcerer etc.)<br /> <br /> As well as a happy helping of Special Abilities that you can just tack on for thematics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T10:30:54-08:00","id":78414,"title":"","content":"A slasher style book on cults would be grand. Maybe even organizations in general - cults, secret societies, conspiracies, etc. <br /> <br /> I think they should do a sequel to Mortal Remains called &quot;Threats Unknown&quot; covering monsters (and their related compacts/conspiracies) not present in the other lines and new to Hunter specifically. This came up in the Mortal Remains title thread. <br /> <br /> The ghouls from the core book's fiction would be the top of my list for coverage in that sort of book, but there are any number of critters from horror fiction they could make use of without having to go through the process of making them viable protagonist characters for a full game line. Say Ghouls, other (purely monstrous) shape changers (were jaguars, wendigo, etc), some kind of ocean based adversary - Kraken and Deep Ones, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T10:51:08-08:00","id":78429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=77598#post77598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter is something I really crave. Many of the Tier 3 groups are potential globe-spanning, and yet the average cell is left to their own devices other than someone passing down new Endowments every once in a while. Feeling like a part of a larger, cohesive body is often missing, and something I really enjoy in play. A focus on making sure your VALKYRIE squad has a home base to report to and debriefings to put up with, having your Lucifuge cell make yearly visits to Milan, or your Cheiron acquisitions team filing reports with their supervisor at the tail end of the week would all be most welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not as much as I would like at the moment. There's a chapter on designing a cult, using the MM as an example (in progress) to fill it full of cool plot hooks and provide more interesting roles to play than the guy who shoots monsters. I don't just mean giving some minor details about each status dot but, my go to example: Remember that scene in Ghostbusters when they meet the mayor of New York and his personal priest comes along and is clearly the one with the most influence. Imagine playing that guy, secretly guiding a major politician to promote the MM (and the Church proper) interests, coving up crimes commuted by the Conspiracy, and protecting him from subversion by monsters. You don't even need to be a fighter, you could have people for that.<br /> <br /> If you've got more ideas, preferably general rather than going through every org, I'd want to hear them. Or stories and fluff, one of the ideas I had was that nearly every story before the section on a Compact or Conspiracy is about internal stuff rather than fighting monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=77598#post77598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum: Something on non-Endowment assets for Tier 2 and 3 play would be really great. Sure, your VALKYRIE cell has Aetheric Rounds in their MP5s, but can they requisition a helicopter or a back-up team? The Union is bound to make friends around town; perhaps one of them is a no-questions-asked surgeon or can get them illegal firearms? This doesn't necessarily have to be enforced by mechanics, but just Storyteller guidelines for making Tier 2 and 3 play feel that much more powerful than just being a lone cell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Start contributing some of them?<br /> <br /> Any ideas? I have a merit called Patron (1 Merit dot becomes 3 floating Merit dots in neat goodies you patron gives you. Drawback, your patron calls the shots.) With the explicit advice that it could be used for your commanding officer in a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=77638#post77638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I second a book about cults. I didn't like the cults presented in Antagonists. Too mundane and low key for me. I would a book about cults in the same style as Slasher.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be pleased to know we're planning some very high-key supernatural cults. Feel free to write some more, we normally divide them into two sections: An overview and storytelling hints, a few paragraphs of each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:54:38-08:00","id":78521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aermas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=77964#post77964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see a book about building monsters with quick &amp; easy package systems. You pick an Attribute pack like (Brusier, Tank, Rake, Socialite, Leader, Wily, Genius) that have pre-constructed Attributes, then you tack on a Skills Package, &amp; Dread Powers Packages like (Werewolf Bezerker, Vampire Charmer, Vampire Predator, Werewolf Shaman, Undead Titan, Dark Sorcerer etc.)<br /> <br /> As well as a happy helping of Special Abilities that you can just tack on for thematics</div> </div> </div> </div>YES. THIS. PLEASE.<br /> <br /> As someone who's about to build 40-odd one off monsters, I'd LOVE something like this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:28:40-08:00","id":80753,"title":"","content":"A book on playing the high-ranking members and leaders of compacts and conspiracies would be something I'd snatch up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","user":"SirPants","date":".  typo 02-28-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:40:26-08:00","id":83731,"title":"","content":"The material in Mummy: the Curse on running a cult (assigning points to Reach and Grasp, deciding the organization of it [Tribal, Conspiracy, or Enterprise], and calling on them for military support) could be expanded into a full system for a larger view of Compacts and Conspiracies. It's neat stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:04:22-08:00","id":84025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SirPants</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=80753#post80753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A book on playing the high-ranking members and leaders of compacts and conspiracies would be something I'd snatch up</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be really cool. I'm imagining a well-guarded room with an Omnipresent Council of Vagueness or a Secret Circle of Circle sitting around deciding how best to handle the latest monster threat - decisions which will affect mundane, human societies at their expense.<br /> <br /> Hunter is a personal game of horror and how much you sacrifice for the Vigil. Top-tier Hunter would be about being too far gone, and now it asks how much you're willing to risk the human world you claim to protect in order to stop the monsters. Now you're a Cheiron board-member (see <i>Compacts &amp; Conspiracies</i> for an 'uh-oh') who is willing to inject vampire blood into a little town in Kansas just to lure out the elder who's been hiding there. Now you're a leader of Aegis Kai Doru hunting down a centuries-old Slavic bloodline of werewolves, killing even the non-werewolves of the family.<br /> <br /> You've made the sacrifice for the Vigil, but is it your right to sacrifice the ignorant for the cause?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:12:30-08:00","id":84029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=78414#post78414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A slasher style book on cults would be grand. Maybe even organizations in general - cults, secret societies, conspiracies, etc.<br /> <br /> I think they should do a sequel to Mortal Remains called &quot;Threats Unknown&quot; covering monsters (and their related compacts/conspiracies) not present in the other lines and new to Hunter specifically. This came up in the Mortal Remains title thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever I hear &quot;Threats Unknown&quot;, I am reminded of X-Com.<br /> <br /> Which would be an excellent Hunter game by it's self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:16:48-08:00","id":84033,"title":"","content":"There was this great thread on RPG.net about basically playing X-Com with Mummies instead of aliens.<br /> <br /> Naturally, I'm planning to include it in Cults <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:17:08-08:00","id":84034,"title":"","content":"I'd like a Hunter book devoted to hunters in other parts of the world. I might have said something before, but if we could get a &quot;Rage Across the World&quot; equivalent for Hunter, I would snap that up in a second. (Provided it wasn't botched up like oWoD's <i>Gypsies</i> was.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:25:43-08:00","id":84041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=84033#post84033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was this great thread on RPG.net about basically playing X-Com with Mummies instead of aliens. Naturally, I'm planning to include it in Cults <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> That same thread is what inspired my AMMUT group. I'd love to see your take on something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:37:54-08:00","id":84048,"title":"","content":"I'd buy that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though I think I'd be profoundly disapointed if it resulted in another 12 or so organisations who <i>didn't</i> feel out of place if you included them in your Vigil game. For Vigil Around the World I'd want the way the vigil operates in different areas to feel different, and the organisations to clearly be a product of their culture.<br /> <br /> My suggestion would be to read a lot of monster hunter / urban fantasy books from different parts of the world and take the mood from them. It's what I did for the Lord Stewards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:47:32-08:00","id":84056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=84048#post84048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd buy that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though I think I'd be profoundly disapointed if it resulted in another 12 or so organisations who <i>didn't</i> feel out of place if you included them in your Vigil game. For Vigil Around the World I'd want the way the vigil operates in different areas to feel different, and the organisations to clearly be a product of their culture. My suggestion would be to read a lot of monster hunter / urban fantasy books from different parts of the world and take the mood from them. It's what I did for the Lord Stewards.</div> </div> </div> </div> So long as we don't get a repeat of Demon Hunter X (&quot;everyone in Asia knows monsters exist and sort of don't mind it; here, take these rules for playing as magical ninjas&quot;), I'd love to see Vigil Across The World. The glimpse at international variations in Blood &amp; Smoke was the highlight of the book for me; expanding that to other gamelines would be so welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:49:55-08:00","id":84057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=84048#post84048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd buy that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though I think I'd be profoundly disapointed if it resulted in another 12 or so organisations who <i>didn't</i> feel out of place if you included them in your Vigil game. For Vigil Around the World I'd want the way the vigil operates in different areas to feel different, and the organisations to clearly be a product of their culture.<br /> <br /> My suggestion would be to read a lot of monster hunter / urban fantasy books from different parts of the world and take the mood from them. It's what I did for the Lord Stewards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.. The Stewards never really appealed to me as a Hunter organization. Not enough skeletons in the closet for a tier 3 organization.<br /> <br /> on a different note, I hope that Mortal Remains updates Slasher up to GMC rule set.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:08:36-08:00","id":84072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=84056#post84056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So long as we don't get a repeat of Demon Hunter X (&quot;everyone in Asia knows monsters exist and sort of don't mind it; here, take these rules for playing as magical ninjas&quot;), I'd love to see Vigil Across The World. The glimpse at international variations in Blood &amp; Smoke was the highlight of the book for me; expanding that to other gamelines would be so welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand why that might not be for everyone but I'd rather have an authentic portrayal of what hunter-like stories are in Japan than something sanitised for my western tastes.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if I'm looking for an authentic and accurate portrayal of what monster hunter stories in Japan are like, the oWoD is the last place I'd look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=84057#post84057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh.. The Stewards never really appealed to me as a Hunter organization. Not enough skeletons in the closet for a tier 3 organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that means I did it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T13:00:46-08:00","id":84159,"title":"","content":"I think that essentialism is what got the OWoD into trouble in the first place. An accurate and authentic portrayal of Hunter-like stories in Japan would be pretty similar to what an authentic hunter-like story in America would be. You get Dracula in Japan too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T13:37:16-08:00","id":84198,"title":"","content":"I don't know. I imagine there'll be enough difference in the tropes and common motifs between american monster hunter stories and Japanese monster hunter stories that you could introduce some real and interesting differences to how the Vigil plays out in Japan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T14:38:03-08:00","id":84224,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a book entirely related to ghosts, the dead, undead, lands of worms and similar; we have a bit of that with the vampire-related book, but honestly I'd like a big book of all fucked up dead things for Vigil. Toss in some mummy and geist-related weirdness and I'd be happy. This in part stems for my love of the oWoD Mediums book and Spectre-cults of W:tO; obviously I don't want them ported into Vigil directly, but I'd really like to see some more ghost/dead thing love. We get a bit in Book of the Dead but man, I want more!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T00:16:26-08:00","id":84443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=84072#post84072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, that means I did it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that implying that they don't have skeletons in the closet or that they are practiced masters at the art of skeleton hiding? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 03-05-2014, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:23:49-08:00","id":84692,"title":"","content":"A bit of both really.<br /> <br /> They hid their skeletons well enough to fool you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They're mild, inoffensive, civil servants who tell you exactly what they're doing, why they're doing it, and where the legitimate democracy government gave them the authority; their skeletons are things you need to think about before you realize their significance, so they take them out the closet and present them as something simple and straight forward which you don't have any reason to think about.<br /> <br /> If I were to summurise the Lord Stewards it would be something like &quot;Diplomats who protect the public by cutting deals with monsters&quot;, if you look at it like that, I'm sure you can see the skeletons. It's mostly implicit, though a few places make it explicit. For example they want the vampires to only bite willing donors and the vampires want to bite whoever looks tasty, so they <i>compromise</i> (but not too much, or they'll never get an agreement in that meeting with the hunters next week).<br /> <br /> <br /> But on the other hand they legitimately don't have any skeletons as bad as as the Ascending One's drug cartels or the MM's torture cellars. They're more on VASCU's level. As I said, I intentionally wrote the Stewards to a different tradition* on Urban Fantasy (Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr Norrell, Rivers of London and Yes Minister are the biggest influences) which do seem to be a bit less dark than Hunter's tradition. Also, at the time I was quite bugged by the fact that governments in Urban Fantasy only ever seemed to fight monsters or run sinister conspiracies, I really wanted to have a government department actually governing.<br /> <br /> So they do cut deals with vampires which protect the vampire's right to feed on human blood if they respect certain limits, but they're doing it because they genuinely believe that's a better way to protect the public from vampires then guns and stakes - and if you're playing the Stewards I recommend that it's at least equal to stakes. If you're not, if you can't make Sir Humphrey Applebee into a worthy antagonist you're not trying.<br /> <br /> <br /> * One of the things I really think Dream Catchers did right is that all four groups are really different from each other, so if you don't like one you should find something to like in one of the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-05-2014, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T06:23:57-08:00","id":85962,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t mind a Hunter supplement focusing on aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T12:22:13-08:00","id":86177,"title":"","content":"Personally (or even impersonally, if you prefer!), I'd really like to see a Hunter supplement that death will hunter cells that find themselves working in small, relatively isolated towns. Recently, Pelgrane Press did an awesome part-supplement called 'Station Duty' that dealt with just such a theme. Obviously, the town itself would be a major part of the story/campaign, with the weirdness, threat and horror inspirations taking their leads from such classics as Silent Hill, Lovecraft's towns, Salem's Lot, Twin Peaks, Hobbs End, Gatlin, Derry, Alan Wake's Bright Falls/Night Springs, etc. The surrounding wilderness could also play a part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:35:29-08:00","id":86895,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness: Small Towns would be very neat.<br /> <br /> My current Demon game is set in such a location (it's inspired by The Prisoner). <br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd like to see a full Chronicle Book update for Hunter. To kill two birds with one stone, it could feature Slashers as the antagonist so they get updated at the same time. <br /> <br /> Anyway, it could revamp the Tactics system to work with Conditions and not be quite as annoyingly fiddly and overburdened (who thought Tactical Fatigue was a good idea?), revise the Endowments, re-do the Code to work with Integrity, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:57:06-08:00","id":86912,"title":"","content":"As I said in the other thread. My vote would be for Cults. Since that leads to organisation vs organisation rather than a group of hunters vs a lone Slasher, and can work with both purely mortal &quot;evil-hunter-like&quot; antagonists and a cult run by a monster. Plus when you get down to it all Slashers have a motivation of &quot;kill X&quot;, cults have more verity.<br /> <br /> The only reason I'm not reworking Cults to do so is that it's a lot of work and I'm one person, and also I wouldn't have much idea how to balance the core 12's chronicle rewrite with the core 12's views on cults","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T20:29:01-07:00","id":90605,"title":"","content":"Isn't that small town stuff already done in Mysterious Places and Midnight Roads?<br /> <br /> I would like to see more of that ten photographs stuff. Maybe in the Chronicle book? It was pretty awesome. A bit like the Shadow, only very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T21:13:07-07:00","id":90628,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd love the following.<br /> <br /> Cults: Even if it's just cults that follow vampires or witches, the guidelines to build entirely original cult concepts appeals to me, and when Kings and I were working on the Cults fanbook we agreed it would be nice to see the darker reflection of the organizations like how Slasher was for individual hunters.<br /> <br /> Aliens/Cryptids/Misc: In the core it's noted that hunters go up against a lot of weird crap, so a book styled like Night Horrors that focuses on said weird crap would be a perfect way to possibly handle this stuff.<br /> <br /> Compact/Conspiracy focused books: Not necessarily a single compact of conspiracy, but more like a book focused on each. Different segments of each, more details/leads on their founders and histories, ways to both get great story hooks and find new antagonists.<br /> <br /> Finally, a Hunter kickstarter. Seriously, if money's a problem, I'm sure I'm not alone in saying I will gladly throw what money I have at this to make it a reality. Please, in anyone who is actually important reads this, some of us are definitely fine with a kickstarter for Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T03:27:08-07:00","id":92209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=90605#post90605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that small town stuff already done in Mysterious Places and Midnight Roads?<br /> <br /> I would like to see more of that ten photographs stuff. Maybe in the Chronicle book? It was pretty awesome. A bit like the Shadow, only very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is now seconded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T15:40:00-07:00","id":175592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkhunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=92209#post92209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is now seconded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadows of the UK had an entire bit on Intersitial Terrain that was a lot like the Ten Photographs material. If I remember right, there's another city that shares the same space occupied by Glasgow. Great stuff; I'd love to see more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T00:50:06-07:00","id":175848,"title":"","content":"well, maybe it is because it's easy to please me, but as long as there are new compacts/ conspiracies in a book, I'm hooked :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T02:32:30-07:00","id":175883,"title":"","content":"My dissapointment with Mortal Remains' demon chapter means I now want a Hunter vs Demons book quite badly.<br /> <br /> Specifically I want a Hunter vs Inferno book that explores, rather than ignores, the Abrahamic themes found in 3 or 4 of the core twelve organisations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T22:06:20-07:00","id":176740,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely like to see Hunter: Cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T13:11:23-07:00","id":177282,"title":"","content":"You should reply to your PM's then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&