rincessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:32:52-07:00","id":184002,"title":"","content":"... No I didn't. Thanks for something that may be obvious in hindsight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T04:55:28-07:00","id":186197,"title":"","content":"Hunter: Crime. You can have jokes about The Union's ties to Mafia, Ascending One's in the cartels, Task-force Valkyrie and possible ties to the Black Market, Cheiron's R and D, Ashwood Abbey getting a world wide contest like the Purge like event happening, and the list goes on and on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T09:26:27-07:00","id":186328,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who doesn't like the historical settings that are so out of touch with today that we can't even relate to them anymore?<br /> <br /> There's so much energy spent filling in the gaps and ignoring the cultural inconsistencies, that it takes the player out of the game. Sure, these books may be a good read, but I have trouble drumming up a crew willing to play a modern day game let alone trying to explain to them the intricacies of a Roman Senate or a Medieval class system.<br /> <br /> If there's a historical setting screaming for Hunter, it would be around the 1950s - 1970s. These decades are still relatable, but there's a different kind of feeling in the world. The Cold War put everyone on edge, and screaming &quot;Communist&quot; in a crowded theater is just as likely to cause a panic as a fire. <br /> <br /> The threat of annihilation by unstoppable powers is looming, and everyone is on edge wanting to protect their family and way of life. <br /> <br /> It would be like modern-day, but it takes away the instant communication/information technology that solves so many of today's Hunter problems. Think &quot;New Wave Requiem&quot; with a Rockabilly edge instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T10:00:55-07:00","id":186362,"title":"","content":"Considering we can still relate to Ancient Sumerians in really significant ways?<br /> <br /> Nah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T13:07:21-07:00","id":186458,"title":"","content":"I'd add; depending on when you were born, the Cold War can sound just as alien as a medieval caste system. A Roman setting is at least radically different enough that it makes the shift in mindset self-evident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T15:29:16-07:00","id":186551,"title":"","content":"If we're going to talk about era's for Hunter; well to me there's only one possibility. World War II<br /> <br /> <br /> This is probably more obvious if you look closely at my homebrew, but to me WWII is the birth of the &quot;modern&quot; vigil. In that pretty much every group tied to a real world group is heavily influenced by WWII, except possibly the MM. After all, WWII did define the modern world.<br /> <br /> So I'd do WWII as the origin story of the modern vigil. You'd see groups like TF:V, KSI29 or MI18 in their younger and perhaps wildly different incarnation. Other groups like VASCU don't exist yet, but you'd see them foreshadowed. For example Nazi proto-Teleinfomatics; (Teleinfomatics mentions that it was created from MKUltra which in turn comes from Operation Paperclip).<br /> <br /> <br /> Not to mention it's a great setting. All that turmoil, who knows what monsters will be awoken by the falling bomb. There's some WWII Hunter stuff in the Sin-Eaters Chapter of Mortal Remains, and it's pretty much what I imagined it could be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T17:55:31-07:00","id":186666,"title":"","content":"If you are going to run a pre-modern Hunter game, how can you ignore the era that started it all? Salem &amp; the new Colonies &amp; Industrialized Europe. Sure WWII has some cool Nazi Occultism &amp; the advent of most modern day technologies &amp; the way we think but it doesn't shout Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T21:05:41-07:00","id":186806,"title":"","content":"WWII is such an overdone setting, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T03:41:35-07:00","id":186955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/77541-books-you-would-like-to-see?p=186806#post186806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WWII is such an overdone setting, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree entirely... WW2 is somewhat too predictable as a setting and has certainly been done to death in recent horror rpg publications (Achtung Cthulhu, Laundry Files backstory, Delta Green, World War Cthulhu). Plus I've noticed that the WW2 stuff seems to have this unbearably kitsch feel to it, all bad English accents (and mustaches) and over the top GIs going into occupied Europe to fight predictably lame mad Nazi scientists/sorcerers/etc. Then again if your gaming group loves WW2, who am I to gainsay you! <br /> <br /> Some juicy historical Hunter settings could include: Eastern/Central Europe during the time of the Wars of the Catholic League Vs the Ottomans (Solomon Kane type era), dark stories told just before/during/after the Spanish Civil War (a nod to Guillermo del Toro and Pan's Labyrinth, as well as the books of <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Carlos Ruiz Zaf\u00f3n and Arturo P\u00e9rez-Reverte</span></span>), Renaissance city states during the era of the Medici's or Borgia's, post WW2 Berlin, the Dust Bowl era, Cold War Soviet era adventures set in the satellite states, India during the time the Great Rebellion 1957, or even a 'Dark Future' neo-noir a la Children of Men/Animatrix/Blade Runner/Hardware (AI machines possessed by inferno demons/god machine anyone/whatever's your poison?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}